title: nemesis1_contact
---
Narrator:
Someone has been here before you.

---

Narrator:
The system shows signs of recent passage — not the slow residue of habitation, but the sharp trace of deliberate transit. Someone moved through here quickly. Recently.

Your navigator estimates within the last six days.

---

Narrator:
There is a message buoy at the transit point.

It is addressed to you. By name.

---

Narrator:
Your security officer advises against activating it. Whatever intelligence operation is running here is more sophisticated than standard doctrine. They knew your approach vector before you did.

Your signals officer says: that's why we should hear what they have to say.

---

-> [Activate the buoy]
    <<apply_effect "nemesis_intel">>
    <<chain_event "nemesis1_ambush">>
    Narrator:
    The message is brief.

    Narrator:
    It says: You are not the first fleet we have watched. You are the first one that concerns us.

    Narrator:
    It says: We will be watching the next system, too. What you do there matters to us.

    Narrator:
    It says nothing else.

    Narrator:
    Your security officer begins compiling a dossier. Whatever this is, it's been running longer than either of you.

-> [Destroy the buoy — leave no trace]
    <<apply_effect "nemesis_curse">>
    Narrator:
    The shaped charge detonates cleanly.

    Narrator:
    Forty minutes later, a second buoy deploys from a concealed cache on the system's outer body.

    Narrator:
    It does not contain a message. It contains a record of you destroying the first one.

    Narrator:
    Someone is keeping notes.

===
